## The Mandate

Adevar Inc. is a high-velocity technical team digitizing the informal restaurant economy across Nigeria and Vietnam via **anra** (a $15/month QR-powered operating system) and **CasperID** (a biometric identity protocol). We do not operate on traditional corporate timelines. We move at an aggressive pace, and we require a creative lead who can match that momentum.

We are seeking a Design & Hype Intern—referred to internally as **"The Megaphone."** Your role is to translate raw data, complex technical architectures, and aggressive sales objectives into high-converting, world-class visual assets with overnight turnaround times.

### The Mission: Visual Authority & Brand Velocity

In a high-growth environment, perception is reality. As we interface with top-tier accelerators (e.g., Y Combinator, Berkeley SkyDeck) and recruit an expansive network of sales Affiliates, your mission is to ensure every visual touchpoint—from investor decks to street-level marketing collateral—reflects the prestige of a global fintech leader.

## Key Responsibilities (The Trenches)

- **Growth Collateral**: Design high-impact, "Street Wealth" style marketing assets for our Affiliate Relationship Managers (RMs) in Lagos and Hanoi.
- **Investor Relations**: Distill complex technical concepts, such as Markov Chain Identity (MCI) algorithms and AI agent integrations, into elegant, intuitive pitch deck slides for venture capital engagement.
- **Rapid UI/UX Prototyping**: Execute high-fidelity Figma mockups for new **anra** features within hours, providing the blueprint for our engineering team to ship code by the following day.
- **The "Propaganda" Engine**: Document the founder’s journey by converting technical updates into high-energy, viral content for LinkedIn and X (Twitter) to drive industry sentiment.

## Candidate Profile

- **Digital Native**: You have a mastery of the "Neo-Fintech" aesthetic—characterized by high contrast, bold typography, and minimalist yet aggressive branding.
- **Momentum-Driven**: You prioritize speed over theoretical perfection. You understand that a functional, high-quality asset delivered today is more valuable than a "perfect" one delivered next week.
- **Tool-Agnostic Mastery**: You are proficient in Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, and video editing software (e.g., CapCut, Premiere). You possess the "figure-it-out" mentality for any new creative tool.
- **High Agency**: You take initiative. If a graphic is outdated or a UI element is suboptimal, you redesign it and present the solution without being prompted.

## Compensation & Professional Upside

- **Monthly Stipend**: A flat retainer to ensure your creative engine remains fueled.
- **Performance Credits**: Cash bonuses for assets that directly lead to investor meetings or significant spikes in Affiliate acquisitions.
- **Elite Portfolio Building**: You will build a live portfolio of work driving revenue and securing international partnerships across two continents, far surpassing academic case studies.

## How to Apply

**Verification**: Navigate to the CasperID portal and ensure your professional profile and resume are securely uploaded.

**Submission**: Click the "Apply" button via the job details page, we will get back to you in 3 working days.

**Bonus Point [The Proposal]**:Send an email to **careers@casperid.com** with the subject line: **"Design Intern: [Your Name]"**.

- **The Teardown**: Select a prominent African or Southeast Asian fintech application. In exactly two sentences, identify the primary weakness in their current UI/UX or branding.
- **The Sprint**: Create a high-energy, "Neo-Fintech" graphic announcing that **anra** has reached 100 active restaurants. (Constraint: Spend no more than 30 minutes on this. Provide a link to the file).
- **The Proof**: A link to your Figma portfolio, Behance profile, or a curated folder of your best UI/UX and graphic design work.

**Adevar Inc: Move Fast. Scale Hard. Own the Future.**
